	"page": {
		"page_Cancellation_Policy_Heading": "Cancellation policy",
		"page_Cancellation_Policy_Text": "Each service provided by TRAVSUS on the present Website (activities, day trips, guided tours and transfers) has its own specific cancellation policy. The User can check each specific cancellation policy in the description part of each activity (in the Website) or on the confirmation email that TRAVSUS will send the User once the reservation has been made. Hence, the specific cancellation conditions will be applicable to each service, which establish the cancellation time and possible penalisation. TRAVSUS will manage cancellations and will confirm the cancellation policies of each activity, excursion, guided tour and/or transfer. If the PROVIDER does not have availability on the reserved date, TRAVSUS will offer the customer an alternate date or schedule, which must be accepted or declined by the customer. If no reply about the alternative option is received within 72 hours, the booking will be cancelled and refunded immediately. In either case, TRAVSUS will send the relevant documentation. IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE ABOVE, AND BY ACCEPTING THESE GENERAL TERMS OF USE, THE USERS DECLARE TO HAVE EXPRESSLY READ AND ACCEPTED THE PRESENT CANCELLATION POLICY AND HEREBY AGREE TO THE CANCELLATION POLICIES OF EACH ACTIVITY, DAY TRIP, GUIDED TOUR AND / OR TRANSFER THAT ARE RESERVED ON THE PRESENT WEBSITE.",
		"page_Guest_Requirements_Heading": "Guest requirements",
		"page_Guest_Requirements_Text": "Up to 100 guests ages 4 and up can attend. Parents may also bring children under 2 years of age.",
		"page_Host_Description": "Providing lake views, The Symphony 9 Tam Coc in Ninh Binh provides accommodation, an outdoor swimming pool, a bar, a shared lounge, a garden and barbecue facilities...",
		"page_Host_Fast_Response": "Fast response - within a few hours",
		"page_Host_Information_Heading": "Host Information",
		"page_Host_Joined_Date": "Joined in March 2016",
		"page_Host_Name": "Kevin Francis",
		"page_Host_Places_Count": "12 places",
		"page_Host_Response_Rate": "Response rate - 100%",
		"page_Itinerary_Heading": "Itinerary",
		"page_Overview_Heading": "Overview",
		"page_Reviews_Heading": "Reviews ({count} reviews)",
		"page_See_Host_Profile_Button": "See host profile",
		"page_Share_Thoughts_Placeholder": "Share your thoughts ...",
		"page_Things_To_Know_Heading": "Things to know",
		"page_Travel_Category_Accessories": "Accessories",
		"page_Travel_Category_Clothing": "Clothing",
		"page_Travel_Category_Cultural_Considerations": "Cultural Considerations",
		"page_Travel_Category_Health_and_Safety": "Health and Safety",
		"page_Travel_Category_Optional_Items": "Optional Items",
		"page_Travel_Category_Special_Activities": "Special Activities",
		"page_Travel_Category_Technology": "Technology",
		"page_Travel_Category_Travel_Essentials": "Travel Essentials",
		"page_Travel_Item_Accessories_1": "Sunscreen and sunglasses: The sun can be intense, especially in desert areas.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Accessories_2": "Wide-brimmed hat or scarf: For sun protection and to cover up when needed.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Accessories_3": "Reusable water bottle: Stay hydrated while being eco-friendly.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Accessories_4": "Daypack: For carrying essentials during day trips.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Clothing_1": "Lightweight, breathable clothes: Cotton or linen for hot days.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Clothing_2": "Modest clothing: Long skirts, dresses, and loose pants are recommended for women.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Clothing_3": "Layers: A light jacket or sweater for cooler evenings and mountain areas.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Clothing_4": "Comfortable shoes: For walking, hiking, and exploring cities like Marrakech and Fez.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Clothing_5": "Swimwear: For beaches, pools, or traditional hammams (spas).",
		"page_Travel_Item_Cultural_Considerations_1": "Small gifts: If invited to someone's home, it's polite to bring a token of appreciation.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Cultural_Considerations_2": "Phrasebook or translation app: Learning a few phrases in Tamazight or French can be helpful.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Health_and_Safety_1": "Basic first-aid kit: Include band-aids, pain relievers, and any prescription medications.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Health_and_Safety_2": "Insect repellent: Useful, especially if visiting during warmer months.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Health_and_Safety_3": "Hand sanitizer and wet wipes: For cleanliness on the go.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Optional_Items_1": "Notebook or journal: To document your experiences.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Optional_Items_2": "Books or e-reader: For downtime during travel.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Special_Activities_1": "Hiking gear: If trekking in the Atlas Mountains or other hiking areas.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Special_Activities_2": "Warm clothing: If visiting the Sahara Desert at night, as temperatures can drop significantly.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Special_Activities_3": "Snorkeling or diving gear: If planning water adventures along the coast.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Technology_1": "Phone and charger: Consider purchasing a local SIM card for affordable internet access.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Technology_2": "Power bank: To keep devices charged during long excursions.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Technology_3": "Camera: To capture Morocco's stunning landscapes and architecture.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Travel_Essentials_1": "Passport and visa (if required): Ensure they are valid for your travel dates.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Travel_Essentials_2": "Travel insurance: For emergencies or unexpected situations.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Travel_Essentials_3": "Cash in Moroccan Dirham (MAD): Many places, especially smaller shops, don't accept cards.",
		"page_Travel_Item_Travel_Essentials_4": "Plug adapter: Morocco uses type C and E plugs, with a voltage of 220V.",
		"page_View_More_Reviews_Button": "View more 20 reviews",
		"page_What_To_Bring_Heading": "What to bring"
	},
